      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "0a2cea42865b97585f7ce9014cfa64bd4e6926f02e99b41ef88bccc835a4f036",
      "text": "Day 2 · After breakfast, sightseeing tour with an English-speaking guide. Begin in the city centre at La Moneda, a national historic monument built in neoclassical style during the last years of Spanish rule to house the royal mint; since the mid-19th century it has been the seat of the Chilean government. Continue to the Plaza de Armas, where the history of the city began, surrounded by the Governor’s House, the City Hall, the Central Post Office, the Royal Audience building and the Cathedral. Climb Santa Lucía Hill for a magnificent panorama, then discover the modern districts of Vitacura, Las Condes and Providencia, driving along the Mapocho River and the city’s main avenues.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1aWUbUU6YPlsMBoyRKpXYQxnELzXegGOR",
        "documentSha256": "cd5c9d0e54f0166e1c3ed8f6c03be635dc44daca3563550e3450f0cca8520dae",
